Q: Hibernate ManyToMany on the same entity results in recursion A: <p>The Hibernate mapping itself looks fine. The recursion you're seeing is almost certainly happening during JSON serialization (Jackson), not in Hibernate itself. When Jackson serializes a DemoEntity, it serializes friends, which each have friendOf pointing back, which have friends, etc. → infinite loop.</p>
<p>You can break the cycle with @JsonIgnore on one side.</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>@ManyToMany
@JoinTable(name = &quot;friends&quot;, joinColumns = @JoinColumn(name = &quot;id1&quot;), inverseJoinColumns = @JoinColumn(name = &quot;id2&quot;))
private List&lt;DemoEntity&gt; friends;

@JsonIgnore  // Don't serialize this side
@ManyToMany
@JoinTable(name = &quot;friends&quot;, joinColumns = @JoinColumn(name = &quot;id2&quot;), inverseJoinColumns = @JoinColumn(name = &quot;id1&quot;))
private List&lt;DemoEntity&gt; friendOf;
</code></pre>
